        <activityName xml:lang="en">Hydrogen production, steam methane reforming of natural gas, with CCS, 25 bar</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Hydrogen production, steam methane reforming of natural gas, with CCS, 25 bar
Natural gas:  0.73 kg/m3 at standard condition @ 15Â°C, 1.03 bar. LHV by mass: 46.5 MJ/kg. LHV by volume at standard condition: 36.0 MJ/Nm3. Post-combusiton carbon capture, based on MDEA technology, with a 98% efficiency. The reformer furnace emissions are not captured. Hence, there is an overall capture rate of 65%. Source: Antonini et al., 2020. Hydrogen production from natural gas and biomethane with carbon capture and storage â€“ A techno-environmental analysis. Sustainable Energy Fuels, 2020,4, 2967-2986. https://doi.org/10.1/D0SE00222D

